\begin{document}

\section{Math color (T1.5)}

Inline known color: $\textcolor{red}{E=mc^2}$ stays inline.

All eight base names: $\textcolor{green}{g}$, $\textcolor{blue}{b}$, $\textcolor{cyan}{c}$, $\textcolor{magenta}{m}$, $\textcolor{yellow}{y}$, $\textcolor{black}{k}$, $\textcolor{white}{w}$.

Unknown color name renders uncolored: $\textcolor{orange}{x+1}$.

Nested inside a fraction the color survives: $\frac{\textcolor{green}{a+b}}{2}$.

Inside a script the color flattens away (scripts are leaves): $x^{\textcolor{red}{2}}$.

Display math:

\[ \textcolor{blue}{\sum_{i=1}^n i} = \frac{n(n+1)}{2} \]

\end{document}
